===Noun===
{{wikipedia|respiration (physiology)}}
{{en-noun|~}}

# The process of [[inhaling]] and [[exhaling]]; [[breathing]], [[breath]].
#* {{quote-book|en|title=An Inquiry Into the Opinions, Ancient and Modern, Concerning Life and Organization|passage=In the dead state all is apparently without motion. No agent within indicates design, intelligence, or foresight: there is no '''respiration'''; […] |year=1822|author=w:John Barclay|page=2|pageurl=https://www.google.ca/books/edition/An_Inquiry_Into_the_Opinions_Ancient_and/YYEwE7FYP14C?hl=en&gbpv=1&pg=PA1|section=I|chapter=I|publisher=Bell & Bradfute; Waugh & Innes; G. & W. B. Whittaker|location=Edinburgh; London|url=https://www.google.ca/books/edition/An_Inquiry_Into_the_Opinions_Ancient_and/YYEwE7FYP14C?hl=en&gbpv=0}}
# An act of [[breathing]]; a [[breath]].
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1931|author=William Faulkner|title=Sanctuary|page=76|publisher=Vintage|year_published=1993
|passage=Gowan snored, each '''respiration''' choking to a huddle fall, as though he would never breathe again.}}
# Any similar process in an organism that lacks [[lungs]] that exchanges [[gas]]es with its [[environment]].
# The process by which [[cell]]s obtain [[chemical]] [[energy]] by the consumption of [[oxygen]] and the release of [[carbon dioxide]].

